      "id": "RCL-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-ray-class-zero-free",
      "title": "Continuation, zero-free region and Landau–Page uniqueness without a functional equation",
      "hypotheses": "A finite abelian group G (written additively with identity 0 ∈ G and character group Ĝ), parameters B ≥ 4 and local class density κ ∈ [1/B, 4] with |G| ≤ B, and nonnegative sequences a, λ : G × ℕ → ℝ_{≥0} satisfying: (1) a(g, 0) = 0, a(0, 1) = 1, and a(g, 1) = 0 for g ≠ 0; (2) |∑_{1≤n≤x} a(g, n) − κx| ≤ 10√x for all g ∈ G and x ≥ 1; (3) |∑_{n≥1} a(g, n) e^{−tn} − κ/t| ≤ B¹⁰ t for all g ∈ G and 0 < t ≤ 1; (4) ∑_{g∈G} λ(g, n) ≤ 2Λ(n) and a(g, n) log n = ∑_{h∈G} ∑_{pq=n} λ(h, p)a(g − h, q) for all g ∈ G and n ≥ 0; and (5) for every real character χ ∈ Ĝ (χ² = 1) and n ≥ 0, ∑_{pq=n} b₁(p)b_χ(q) ≥ 0 and ∑_{pq=n²} b₁(p)b_χ(q) ≥ b₁(n), where b₁(p) = ∑_{g∈G} a(g, p) and b_χ(q) = ∑_{g∈G} (Re χ(g))a(g, q).",
      "statement": "For every χ ∈ Ĝ, the Mellin continuation F(χ, s) is holomorphic on Re s > 1/2, equals (s − 1)^{𝟏_{χ=1}} ∑_{n≥1} a_χ(n)n^{−s} on Re s > 1, satisfies ‖F(χ, s)‖ ≤ 300B(‖s‖ + 1)² on Re s ≥ 11/20, obeys F(χ, s̄) = conj(F(χ, s)) when χ² = 1, and satisfies F(χ, s) ≠ 0 and −F′(χ, s)/F(χ, s) + 𝟏_{χ=1}/(s − 1) = ∑_{n≥1} λ_χ(n)n^{−s} on Re s > 1. Moreover, with ℓ(t) = log(B(|t| + 2)), there exist absolute constants c₁, c₂ > 0 such that across all such L-families: (a) every zero s of F(χ, ·) with Re s ≥ 3/4 and (χ² ≠ 1 or Im s ≠ 0) satisfies Re s < 1 − c₁/ℓ(Im s); and (b) if χ² = ψ² = 1 and β, β′ ≥ max(3/4, 1 − c₂/ℓ(0)) satisfy F(χ, β) = F(ψ, β′) = 0, then χ = ψ, β = β′, and F′(χ, β) ≠ 0.",
      "definitions": [
        "abstract finite-abelian-group L-family (B ≥ 4, class density κ ∈ [1/B, 4])",
        "twisted Dirichlet coefficients a_χ(n) and λ_χ(n)",
        "Mellin remainder integral M(χ, s) and regularized continuation F(χ, s)",
        "conductor-height weight ℓ(t) = log(B(|t| + 2))",
        "concentric-disc Blaschke and Borel–Carathéodory local logarithmic derivative"
      ],
