      "title": "Truncated Perron contour shift and the explicit formula with an exceptional zero",
      "hypotheses": "0 < c₀ ≤ 1/20; an abstract finite-abelian-group L-family with scale B ≥ 4; a character χ ∈ Ĝ; a finite set Z ⊂ ℝ satisfying the c₀-admissible exceptional-zero specification (|Z| ≤ 1, every β ∈ Z satisfies 1 − c₀/ℓ(0) ≤ β < 1, F(χ, β) = 0 and F′(χ, β) ≠ 0, and every zero w of F(χ, ·) with Re w ≥ 1 − c₀/ℓ(Im w) lies in Z); and a real number u ≥ 2 with log B ≤ √(log u).",
      "statement": "There exist constants c, C > 0 depending only on c₀ such that ψ(χ, u) = ∑_{1≤n≤u} λ_χ(n) satisfies ‖ψ(χ, u) − 𝟏_{χ=1} u + ∑_{β∈Z} u^β / β‖ ≤ C u exp(−c√(log u)).",
      "definitions": [
        "c₀-admissible exceptional zero set Z ⊂ ℝ",
        "half-width zero-free corridor 1 − c₀/(2ℓ(Im s)) ≤ Re s ≤ 3",
        "truncated Perron abscissa σ₀ = 1 + 1/log u and height T = exp((c₀/32)√(log u))",
        "pigeonhole left vertical abscissa σ₁ ∈ [1 − 4d, 1 − 2d] at step d = c₀/(8ℓ(T))"
      ],
