      "correspondence": "Subtracting the local zero sum in B̄(5/4 + i Im s, 3/5) bounds F′/F − ∑_{β∈Z} 1/(s − β) by O(ℓ(Im s)²) on Re s ≥ 1 − c₀/(2ℓ(Im s)). At W = √(log u), δ = c₀/32 and T = exp(δW) (with Chebyshev fallback when δW ≤ 1), a two-line pigeonhole choice selects σ₁ ∈ [1 − 4d, 1 − 2d] at distance ≥ d = c₀/(8ℓ(T)) from Z, and shifting the truncated Perron integral across [σ₁, σ₀] × [−T, T] extracts 𝟏_{χ=1} u − ∑_{β∈Z} u^β/β up to O(u exp(−c√(log u))).",
